{"id": "a19", "question": "What is the postfix form of the sample input A+B*C in the stack experiment?", "answerable": true, "error": null, "status": "answered", "reason": "grounded", "answer": "To convert the infix expression A+B*C to postfix, we scan the expression from left to right, pushing operands directly to the output and operators to the output when necessary [S1]. For the operator '+', we pop operators of higher or equal precedence (in this case, '*' and 'A') before pushing '+' [S1]. The resulting postfix expression is ABC*+ [S1].", "best_score": 0.7575, "support": 0.857, "retrieved": [{"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 3, "score": 0.7575}, {"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 5, "score": 0.5833}, {"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 2, "score": 0.5828}], "citations": [{"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 3, "section": "EXPERIMENT 3 - STACK AND INFIX TO POSTFIX CONVERSION"}], "attestation_index": 280, "isolated": false, "ttft_s": 0.5307385000050999, "total_s": 2.556, "hit": true, "citation_correct": [true], "keyword_match": true}
